SUMMARY:Live Music Night: Folkloric Rhythms from Cuba to Colombia
DESCRIPTION:A concert and talk geared to be enjoyed by music enthusiasts\, 
 beginner musicians and professionals alike. Let's gather around a shared l
 ove of music and connect through learning about the diasporic influence of
  “clave” from west Africa throughout the Americas.Los Transplantes: An
  electrifying mix of salsa\, Cuban timba\, Afro Colombian folklore\, hard 
 hitting hip hop\, erudite jazz\, and booty shaking dance music\, Los Trans
 plantes is an explosive New York City trio here to present a bold new soun
 dtrack for the real all American diaspora. Musicians Puli\, Alex\, and Bra
 hm channel their extensive and diverse musical backgrounds into a fiercely
  unified\, genre-bending sound. Their message seeks to break down cultural
  division and deliver an undeniable celebration of unity\, hope\, and resi
 lience. The powerhouse band ignites every stage they hit\, with an infecti
 ous energy that instantly draws crowds to the dance floor\, propelling anc
 ient tradition into a modern and accessible experience for all to be a par
 t of. &nbsp\;From an anthropological perspective\, following the transatla
 ntic slave trade and its unprecedented combination of indigenous cultures\
 , learn how Los Transplantes think about traditional similarities and our 
 global connection to rhythm. We’re all much more similar than we tend to
  think. What does Guinean music have to do with John Coltrane? Everything!
  Haitian Konpa\, Cuban Timba\, and Colombian Cumbia?Evening Flow7:00 PM 
 — Doors open. Settle in\, grab a drink\, and meet a friend.7:30 PM — T
 he evening begins: an opening set with song-by-song explorations led by Lo
 s Transplantes8:30 PM — Intermission and Mingling9:00 PM — Encore!&nbs
 p\;10:00 PM — Last call at the bar as we wind down the evening.This show
  will be a mix of seated and standing room. Come on time if you'd like a c
 hair.&nbsp\;What Is Think Olio?Think Olio is an ongoing experiment in life
 long learning. We are a community of open-minded people who gather to exch
 ange ideas with new friends and connect over art\, literature\, and philos
 ophy.Check out our full calendarOur $30 membership gives you two events fo
 r the price of one!&nbsp\;An Olio is what we call the social learning even
 ts we’ve been organizing since 2015. A blend between a lecture and a hou
 se party\, Olios are led by a teacher who loves sharing their passions and
  the room is filled with curious\, open-minded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;Our goal
  is to spark new perspectives\, ignite curiosity\, and enjoy ourselves soc
 ially\, an alternative to typical nightlife options.Disclaimer: By purchas
 ing a ticket\, you agree to have your photo/video used for social media/ma
 rketing materials. If you prefer to not have your photo taken\, feel free 
 to send us a note. Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n\nTickets & info: https://www.vi
 ewcy.com/event/olio_concert_a_globa
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio_concert_a_globa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f8e95d74-30c0-4a47-be07-f945bd48ffaf@viewcy.olio
DTSTAMP:20261002T175338Z
