SUMMARY:Daddy Energy\, According to the Bhagavad Gita: An Olio Member Salon
DESCRIPTION:Olio Salons are by members for members. Generated by a passion 
 from someone in our community these are social events that create discussi
 on and learning about a new topic each time. To attend this salon you can 
 sign up for our monthly membership which gives you two\, $35 credits to us
 e towards Olio events each month. &nbsp\;&nbsp\;Daddy Energy\, According t
 o the Bhagavad Gita led by member\, Rishi Ishairzay.A 2\,000-year-old less
 on on owning your gifts and sharing them with others. All genders (Baddies
  included) are welcome.Think about it - if all your loved ones acted boldl
 y on their gifts\, and shared them with others - wouldn’t the world be a
  way better place? Filled with more books\, dinner parties\, and more of y
 our friends' weird side projects. That’s the world I want to live in.So 
 why don’t we? For many of us\, the hurdle is putting ourselves out there
  and becoming open to the universe saying “no”. That fear has most peo
 ple shy away from their gifts\, even though the universe might’ve been m
 ore receptive (if only it had been asked!).&nbsp\;Instead of trying to get
  more confident\, we’ll be working with Daddy Energy\, a shift from "wha
 t will they think of me?" to "you are all my children\, and I am here to n
 ourish you." When you’re focused on giving your gifts instead of being a
 pproved of\, a “no” stings a whole lot less.&nbsp\;This idea goes way 
 back. In the Bhagavad Gita\, an ancient Hindu text on living in alignment\
 , the warrior Arjuna freezes on the battlefield because he’s too afraid 
 to act. Krishna's advice to him is what finally gets him unstuck - "You're
  entitled to your actions\, but never to their fruits." In other words\, y
 our job is to devote yourself to what’s true to you\, and let go of atta
 chments to the outcome.In this workshop we’ll use a combination of small
  group discussions\, somatic inquiry\, and a “group cringe session” to
  help you tap into your Daddy Energy and do the thing you always said you 
 wanted to do. We’ll use passages from the Bhagavad Gita to ground the co
 nversation.Expect to walk out of this workshop nourished by the group\, a 
 little emotionally raw\, and stoked to act on that scary and exciting drea
 m of yours.Note: Bring your favorite notebook + pen!&nbsp\;Evening flow7:0
 0 PM – Doors open. Settle in\, grab a drink\, and meet someone new.7:30 
 PM – The Olio begins: a short talk on Daddy Energy and the story of Arju
 na on the battlefield. In pairs\, we discuss the gift we’d want to share
 .8:15 PM – We talk about what fear is and how it can be harnessed\, then
  face it together in a group cringe session.9:00 PM – Step into your Dad
 dy Energy and leave with one concrete next step\, plus a group of Olioites
  cheering you on.9:30 PM – Wind down to a social hour.Want to be the nex
 t member to lead a salon night? Send us a note!&nbsp\;Hi@olio.rsvp&nbsp\;\
 n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/daddy_energy_accordi
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/daddy_energy_accordi
END:VEVENT
