SUMMARY:Olio Sound Salon: DeBÍ TiRAR MáS FOToS
DESCRIPTION:Introducing the Olio Sound Salon!&nbsp\;The premise is simple:O
 ne album.&nbsp\;On vinyl.&nbsp\;Start to finish.&nbsp\;No skips.&nbsp\;As 
 the artist intended.&nbsp\;You and your peoples + new friends&nbsp\;Chat. 
 Dance. Sing.Run of showWe'll start the evening with some question prompts 
 over drinks at the bar and get settled into the room. Rob will give a brie
 f intro to the record and share some miscellaneous records that connect to
  or inspired Bad Bunny's Debí Tirar Más Fotos. We'll spin the album in i
 ts entirety while leaving room for questions and conversation throughout. 
 One room will be dedicated to listening and the other to dancing and chatt
 ing.After the album\, you'll get a list of tracks and albums that relate t
 o Debí Tirar Más Fotos\, so you'll have anti-algorithm sources straight 
 from a DJ to keep your musical deep dive going after the event.About Rob\,
  our DJ and Facilitator for the evening:Robert Michelin is a native Brookl
 ynite\, educator\, percussionist\, ethnomusicologist\, avid record collect
 or\, and father.He earned his MMus in Ethnomusicology at the University of
  London and his MS in Education at Brooklyn College\, and began his post-s
 econdary studies as an Eph at Williams College.As a performing artist\, he
  has shared the stage with Bernard Woma\, Obo Addy\, KweYao Agyapon\, Paul
  Winter\, the Mujuru brothers\, Sekou Sundiata\, David Pleasant\, Abby Dob
 son\, Tito Fuentes\, and Crispin Robinson\, to name a few. His artistic mi
 ssion is to help us understand that we have more in common than we have di
 fferences.What Is an Olio?Think Olio is an ongoing experiment in lifelong 
 learning. We are a community of open-minded people who gather to exchange 
 ideas with new friends and connect over art\, literature\, and philosophy.
 Check out our full calendarOur $30 membership gives you two events for the
  price of one!&nbsp\;An Olio is what we call the social learning events we
 ’ve been organizing since 2015. A blend between a lecture and a house pa
 rty\, Olios are led by a teacher who loves sharing their passions and the 
 room is filled with curious\, open-minded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;Our goal is t
 o spark new perspectives\, ignite curiosity\, and enjoy ourselves socially
 —an alternative to typical nightlife options.Disclaimer: By purchasing a
  ticket\, you agree to have your photo/video used for social media/marketi
 ng materials. If you prefer to not have your photo taken\, feel free to se
 nd us a note. Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.
 com/event/olio_sound_salon_deb
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio_sound_salon_deb
END:VEVENT
